From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: an analysis transform is handed its output after drawing

An ID2D1AnalysisTransform's ProcessAnalysisResults was never called, so an
analysis effect never got its results: Paint.NET 5.2's own Histogram effect
(three compute passes and an analysis pass) left its HistogramOutput null and
Auto-Level failed with "Unexpected null". As Direct2D does: after a
transform that is also an analysis transform is drawn, its output is handed
to it on the CPU, row after row, in the buffer it asked for with
SetOutputBuffer (8-bit BGRA, 16-bit unorm or float, 32-bit float; 4 channels
or 1), and it is drawn whole, whatever part of it shows. An analysis compute
shader writes a RWStructuredBuffer<float> at u0 and Direct2D's constants are
then the inputs' sceneToInputNX/Y only, as Paint.NET's shader declares them;
a draw transform's output texture is read back. A compute transform's output
texture is 32-bit float when it asks for 32BPC_FLOAT.
---
--- a/dlls/d2d1/effect_render.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/effect_render.c
@@ -1031,8 +1031,12 @@
  * scene pixels), int2 outputOffset (added with resultRect.xy to a thread's id to address the output
  * texture: here the texture is the rectangle, so -resultRect.xy), then per input float2 sceneToInputNX,
  * sceneToInputNY (texel = scene * [0] + [1], normalised). */
